module

public import Linglib.Logic.Assignment
public import Linglib.Semantics.Dynamic.DPL.Context
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Submonoid.Basic
public import Mathlib.Data.Set.Piecewise

/-!
# Visser (1998): Contexts in Dynamic Predicate Logic

This file formalizes the parts of Visser's theory of contexts that the substrate
`DPL/Context.lean` leaves to the paper. A context types a relation between assignments by the
variables it reads, the variables at which it cuts the link between input and output value,
and the variables it constrains in the output. Through the agreement relations on assignments,
a relation has a context exactly when [it is its own saturation by agreement on the inputs and
on the outputs, within agreement off the blocks](##hasContext_iff_eq). The relations generated
under composition by the resets and the finitely restricted conditions, the DPL-expressible
ones, [all have a context](##exists_hasContext), with no reference to a language.

## Implementation notes

Variables are natural numbers and the domain is a type parameter. The DPL-expressible relations
are the submonoid of the composition monoid generated by the resets and the finitely restricted
conditions; the identity, the condition restricted to no variable, is among the generators.

